      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to find a zero of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]\u2286{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2 \\\\ {x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting  at the point $[1,\\,1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration, rounding your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n| $[$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$ | {{field-2}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-3}} | $3$ | $-1$ |  |  |  |\n\n| ${x}_{1}\u2248[$ | $0.833$ | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-4}} |  |  |"
